## 2. System shape

```text
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Mobile app         │
│  Expo / React Native│
└──────────┬──────────┘
           │ HTTPS JSON
┌──────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐
│  API (FastAPI)                              │
│  auth · portfolio · catalogue · recommend   │
└──────┬───────────────────────┬──────────────┘
       │                       │
┌──────▼──────────┐   ┌────────▼────────────────┐
│ PostgreSQL      │   │ Worker                  │
│ users, rules,   │   │ crawl · extract · embed │
│ chunk text      │   │ change detect · review  │
└──────▲──────────┘   └────────┬────────────────┘
       │                       │
       │              ┌────────▼────────┐
       │              │ ChromaDB        │
       │              │ 768-d vectors   │
       │              └────────▲────────┘
       │                       │
       │              ┌────────▼────────┐
       │              │ Official bank   │
       └──────────────│ pages and PDFs  │
                      └─────────────────┘
```

Chroma is a persistent store on a shared disk, opened by the API and the worker. It is not an extension inside PostgreSQL. The collection in use is `chunks__bge_base_en_v15`, cosine space. PostgreSQL does not store embedding columns.

Six layers from the PRD map to these deployable pieces:

| PRD layer | Runtime piece |
|---|---|
| Data collection | Worker crawlers, HTML fetch, PDF download |
| Document processing | Worker extractors writing draft rules |
| RAG knowledge base | Hugging Face embeddings, ChromaDB, retrieval in section 7 |
| Structured reward database | PostgreSQL tables in section 4 |
| Deterministic recommendation engine | Pure Python module called by `POST /recommendations` |
| Mobile application | Expo app in `apps/mobile` |

The recommendation request path does not crawl the web. It reads verified rules already in PostgreSQL and returns in the target of under 3 seconds.

