## 9. HTTP API

Base path `/v1`. Authenticated routes use a bearer access token. Errors use `{ "error": { "code", "message" } }`.

### Auth

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/v1/auth/register` | Email or phone, password |
| POST | `/v1/auth/login` | Email or phone plus password. A Gmail-only account is told to continue with Gmail |
| POST | `/v1/auth/google` | Body `{ "id_token" }`. Verifies a Google ID token, requires a verified `@gmail.com` or `@googlemail.com` address, and returns access and refresh tokens. Creates the account when the address is new. Links to an existing email account when one is already there |
| POST | `/v1/auth/otp/request` | Sends OTP to a verified phone transport |
| POST | `/v1/auth/otp/verify` | Exchanges OTP for tokens |
| POST | `/v1/auth/password/reset` | Reset flow |
| POST | `/v1/auth/refresh` | Rotate refresh token |
| DELETE | `/v1/me` | Account deletion |
| GET | `/v1/me/export` | JSON export of profile, cards, recommendations |

### Catalogue and portfolio

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/v1/issuers` | Banks in the supported set |
| GET | `/v1/cards?q=&issuer_id=` | Search by product name or bank; `live` cards only |
| GET | `/v1/cards/{id}` | Name, image, summary, last verified date, source links |
| GET | `/v1/me/cards` | Portfolio |
| POST | `/v1/me/cards` | Body `{ "card_product_id", "nickname?" }` |
| PATCH | `/v1/me/cards/{user_card_id}` | Body `{ "nickname" }`. Empty string clears it |
| DELETE | `/v1/me/cards/{user_card_id}` | Remove from portfolio |

### Recommendation

`POST /v1/recommendations`

```json
{
  "amount_rupees": "10000.00",
  "category_code": "shopping",
  "channel": "online",
  "merchant_name": "Amazon"
}
```

`amount_rupees` is a decimal string. The API converts to paise with half-up to the nearest paisa and rejects values below ₹1 or above ₹10,000,000. `category_code` is required. `merchant_name` is optional; the API resolves it through `merchant_aliases` and still uses `category_code` when the alias is unknown. Unknown merchants do not fail the request.

Response includes `recommendation_id`, the ranked cards, the winner, assumptions, source URLs, `engine_version`, and optional `explanation`. Latency budget for the engine plus DB read is 3 seconds, excluding a slow explanation call, which is capped at 2 seconds and then dropped.

### Internal (not in the mobile app)

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/internal/review/rules?status=needs_review` | Queue for verification |
| POST | `/internal/review/rules/{id}` | `{ "verification_status": "verified" \| "rejected" }` |

Internal routes require a separate staff credential.

