## 12. Security

- TLS everywhere. PostgreSQL and the Chroma directory are encrypted at rest via the host disk encryption. Chroma is not reachable except through the API and the worker. It has no public port.
- Passwords hashed with Argon2. OTPs are single use, 5-minute TTL, rate limited.
- Access tokens are short lived (15 minutes). Refresh tokens are rotated and stored hashed.
- Staff review tools are on a separate auth realm.
- Logs omit phone numbers and email where a user id is enough. Raw bank HTML is stored in the bucket, not in application logs.
- No fields exist for card number, CVV, PIN, expiry, or bank password. Request validation rejects body keys named like those if a client sends them.
- Account delete removes `users`, `user_cards`, sessions, and recommendation rows for that user. Catalogue data stays.

---

## 13. Delivery slices

Each slice is shippable to staging. Mobile and API land together when the slice has a user-visible behaviour.

| Slice | Outcome | Done when |
|---|---|---|
| 0. Foundations | Compose stack, migrations, health check, CI running engine tests | `docker compose up` serves `/health` and an empty engine test passes |
| 1. Auth and profile | Register, login, refresh, reset, delete, export | A user can sign in and call `/v1/me` |
| 2. Catalogue read | Issuers and card search over seeded `live` rows entered by hand | Search by bank and by name returns the seed set |
| 3. Portfolio | Add and remove cards | A user can save two cards from the same bank |
| 4. Engine | Calculation module and golden tests | PRD worked example and cap/exclusion cases pass |
| 5. Recommend API and result UI | End-to-end recommendation on hand-verified rules | p95 under 3 seconds on staging for a 5-card portfolio, explanation optional |
| 6. Ingestion | Allowlisted fetch, hash change detection, draft rules | A changed fixture document produces `needs_review` rows and does not replace verified rows |
| 7. Review and citations | Staff verify flow, source URL on each result, freshness label | A rule cannot reach the app without `verified` and a source URL |
| 8. RAG assist | Chunking, embeddings, retrieval used by reviewers and explanation citations | A result can show the source sentence for the winning rule |

Slices 0–5 are the user-facing MVP core. Slices 6–8 are the knowledge-base MVP from the PRD. Hand-verified seed rules in slice 2 let the app run before crawl is finished.

