## 14. Testing

| Layer | What |
|---|---|
| Engine unit tests | Base earn, category acceleration, merchant override, online vs offline, exclusion, threshold, cap clamp, points-to-paise, tie-break, empty portfolio |
| Golden file | At least 50 cases with expected paise, including the two-card example in section 8.5. Target: 100% on this file before release, which is the practical stand-in for the PRD's 98% accuracy target |
| Chunker tests | Heading split, paragraph split, token-window overlap of 120, table kept whole, table header repeated when a table is split, short chunk merged, PDF page boundary, `chunker_version` bump changes ids |
| Retrieval tests | A chunk for card B is excluded when the filter is card A. Overlap twins collapse at cosine 0.95. Fusion ranks a passage that is both lexically and semantically close above a dense-only neighbour. A rule with stored quote offsets does not call the index. An audit miss forces `needs_review` |
| API tests | Auth, portfolio uniqueness, recommendation validation, unknown merchant still returns a category-based result, explanation timeout still returns the ranked table |
| Worker tests | Unchanged hash does not re-extract. Raw change with the same `text_hash` skips chunk and extract. A quote that is not a substring stays `needs_review`. A verified row survives a new draft |
| Mobile | Detox or Maestro smoke: register, add card, recommend, read winner and source link |

A calculation change bumps `engine_version` and must keep the golden file green or update expected values in the same change with a reviewer.

