## 15. Observability

- Request log on `POST /recommendations`: `recommendation_id`, `latency_ms` through the engine, `citation_ms`, `explanation_ms`, `citation_degraded`, card count, winner `card_product_id`, `engine_version`. No purchase narrative in logs beyond amount bucket (under ₹1k, ₹1k–₹10k, above ₹10k).
- Worker metrics: fetches, hash changes, `text_unchanged` skips, chunks written, embed failures, extraction failures, rows waiting in `needs_review`.
- Alert when a `live` card has `last_verified_at` older than 45 days, and when the review queue exceeds 20 rules.

---

## 16. What this plan leaves for later

Phase 2 in the PRD (cap consumption over the month, milestones, user-set redemption values, spending insights) needs new tables for tracked spend and a user preference for `redemption_values`. The engine's cap step already takes a headroom number; Phase 2 replaces "full cap" with remaining headroom. Phase 3 natural-language queries sit in front of the same `POST /recommendations` contract once category and merchant can be parsed from a sentence. The ranker does not change.
